%S A401948 1,1,2,3,4,6,8,11,15,20,26,35,45,58,74,95,119,150,186,233,287,354,432,
%T A401948 529,643,780,940,1133,1357,1628,1940,2311,2741,3248,3834,4527,5321,
%U A401948 6250,7318,8563,9987,11650,13542,15733,18235,21118,24396,28173,32463,37376,42952,49321,56529
%N A401948 Number of distinct sets of line sizes determined by n points in the real plane.
%C A401948 This is F(n) in Erdős Problem 607.
%C A401948 For a set P of points, the set of line sizes is obtained by counting the points of P on each line that contains at least two points of P.
%H A401948 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A401948/b401948.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A401948 Thomas F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/607">Erdős Problem 607</a>, Erdős Problems.
%H A401948 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sylvester-Gallai theorem">Sylvester-Gallai theorem</a>.
%F A401948 Let b(n) be the number of integer tuples (s_1, ..., s_r) with r >= 2 and 3 <= s_1 < ... < s_r for which Sum_{i=1..r} max(0, s_i + i - r) <= n. a(n) = max(1, n-1) + b(n) for n >= 1.
%F A401948 From _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 13 2026: (Start)
%F A401948 a(n) ~ c * d^sqrt(n) / n^(1/4), where d = 7.8596381305449004514... and c = 0.04253522165995491977...
%F A401948 Conjecture: d = exp(sqrt(Pi^2/3 + 2*log(2)^2)) = 7.8596381305449004514433935377... (End)
%e A401948 a(4) = 3. The possible sets of line sizes are {4}, {2,3} and {2}:
%e A401948   o-o-o-o        o         o-o
%e A401948                 /|\        |X|
%e A401948                o-o-o       o-o
%e A401948     {4}        {2,3}       {2}
%Y A401948 Row sums of A401947.
%K A401948 nonn,new
%O A401948 1,3
%A A401948 _Seiichi Manyama_, Nov 09 2026
